			},
			"date": "2023-12-21T21:34:37.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It's interesting, I never got into Mastodon. I'm sort of trying, I guess, but it's not flying. Who should I follow and where do I find them? I hate being part of an instance. Surfacing of content is lacking, which is a feature as much as a bug. I'm stumped. I mean, I don't need a social network at all, but it's nice to chat a bit, and sometimes dive deeper into an interesting or important discussion. To me, here, the hurdle is huge. That's probably a huge deal to the non-techy masses.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
